{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f59d12bdbc836d549fafe5d8216e1c4932cf879473d596efcb6c9157166d3f2c", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:01TW:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nOver a locally Noetherian base, finite type is finite presentation.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-noetherian-finite-type-finite-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e055b6f73f9e013abc97b9c60ceb7e6468434e2802d6b3bb4e0ead9b9c68885e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e93712d06efcc790e97f37728745f43b53cd56f54bac056b595b89e09b07c5d3", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is locally Noetherian and <MATH_0003> locally of finite type\nthen <MATH_0004> is locally of finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is locally Noetherian and <MATH_0006> of finite type\nthen <MATH_0007> is of finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f35131b3c42aac154cce86fb94d8a7965dd284ec1fea00f7f8deecdecf0facc", "unit_id": "tag:01TX:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Noetherian-finite-type-is-finite-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-Noetherian-quasi-separated}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-finite-presentation-finite-type}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b229ab74d0b2611f376c2d1845de2c6123c72ba2c7b222e3c086ecc99515a184", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f2deb6b1403de664495aad8a0913962cca1309ccfcef088a649c2dbe181c8ee", "source_text": "The first statement follows from the fact that a ring\nof finite type over a Noetherian ring is of finite presentation, see Algebra,\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nSuppose that <MATH_0001> is of finite type and <MATH_0002> is locally Noetherian.\nThen <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact and locally of finite presentation by (1).\nHence it suffices to prove that <MATH_0004> is quasi-separated.\nThis follows from Lemma <REF_0002>\n(and Lemma <REF_0003>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1739955d8b5a320a75ff616f0afc68e8f2aff0ed5e4f1deff6baf94b477cc68", "unit_id": "tag:01TX:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-presentation-quasi-compact-quasi-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4453ad2ec97127c15cdb6391666555ea6663b80384aa571d5636bb49de2e2bec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a01aa1275f622c108858540f02366cfc87b1c589b6fb6889b5c201e9b7d5d669", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme which is quasi-compact and quasi-separated.\nIf <MATH_0002> is of finite presentation over <MATH_0003>, then <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact\nand quasi-separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ecd7a220bdcfe46e8b0589be963ed13b40e6d9377acfac783a90d3492656660b", "unit_id": "tag:01TY:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f59d12bdbc836d549fafe5d8216e1c4932cf879473d596efcb6c9157166d3f2c", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:01TY:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$Y$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-presentation-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8be93d8ba93ee539b593841d2bd7be06f576e7776bf3da832dc8eb61f8703fe7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:584ee6f84f514b6ae0ab5cb565c4f84388a19cefad66a7d062855e51dbf7e6d2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes over <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0003> is locally of finite presentation over <MATH_0004> and\n<MATH_0005> is locally of finite type over <MATH_0006>, then <MATH_0007> is locally\nof finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0008> is of finite presentation over <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010> is quasi-separated\nand locally of finite type over <MATH_0011>, then <MATH_0012> is of finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc9c159b9818876d7dcfef455a1edab72a154b3a558d11824ec9eebd507f5865", "unit_id": "tag:02FV:statement"}
